      "article_sections": [
        {
          "text": "What Is Coffee Filter Packaging?",
          "level": "h2"
        },
        {
          "text": "Coffee filter packaging is designed for single-serve coffee packed inside paper filters. Instead of measuring coffee every morning, customers simply open a filter pack and brew. These products are popular because they're quick, mess-free, and easy to use. Good [coffee packaging](https://hofpack.com/custom-coffee-packaging) keeps every filter clean, protects the coffee from moisture, and helps preserve its fresh aroma until it's ready to brew. No need to worry about chemical leakage or cardboard-like taste with high-quality and sealed coffee filter packaging. ",
          "level": "p"
        },
        {
          "text": " What's The Difference Between Paper And Metal Coffee Filters?\n",
          "level": "h2"
        },
        {
          "text": "Paper filters trap more oils and fine particles than plastic filters. They give a cleaner, lighter-bodied cup. Whereas, metal filters let more oils and micro-grounds through, which produces a slightly heavier brew with more texture. Paper filters are disposable, environmentally friendly, and used once, but metal filters are reusable and long-term, though they need regular cleaning.\n",
          "level": "p"
        },
        {
          "text": " How To Choose Coffee Filters For Your Brewing Method?\n",
          "level": "h2"
        },
        {
          "text": "Filter choice depends on your brewer. Drip machines and pour-over setups typically use paper cone or basket filters sized to the brewer. French press and percolators use built-in metal mesh filters. Espresso machines don't use a separate filter at all — the puck itself acts as the filtering medium. Always match the filter shape and size to your specific machine, since an ill-fitting filter can cause overflow or weak extraction.\n",
          "level": "p"
        },
        {
          "text": "Which Materials Do You Offer?\n",
          "level": "h2"
        },
        {
          "text": "We use durable, food-safe packaging materials designed for coffee products. Choose from our premium material library depending on your product and shipping needs. If sustainability matters to your brand, you’re in luck. Because we also offer eco-friendly material options, such as:\n- Paperboard\n- Kraft paper\n- Corrugated stock\n",
          "level": "p"
        },
        {
          "text": "Why Choose HOF Pack?\n",
          "level": "h2"
        },
        {
          "text": "We understand coffee packaging because we've worked with brands across the industry. Our team helps you create packaging that's easy to use, looks great on the shelf, and protects your product from start to finish. Contact us at info@hofpack.com or call +1 (888) 429-4881 for a free consultation. ",
          "level": "p"
        }
      ]
